    {
      "id": "set-timer-8ff120",
      "name": "SetTimer",
      "category": "TimerManager",
      "signature": "SetTimer(Target, In Out Handle, In Obj, In Timer Method, In Rate, Inb Loop, In First Delay)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FTimerManager*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Out Handle",
          "type": "FTimerHandle&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Obj",
          "type": "UserClass*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Timer Method",
          "type": "FTimerDelegate::TMethodPtr<UserClass>"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Rate",
          "type": "Float"
        },
        {
          "name": "Inb Loop",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "false"
        },
        {
          "name": "In First Delay",
          "type": "Float",
          "default": "-1.f"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<class UserClass> void",
      "docs": "Sets a timer to call the given native function at a set interval.  If a timer is already set\nfor this handle, it will replace the current timer.\n@param InOutHandle\t\t\tIf the passed-in handle refers to an existing timer, it will be cleared before the new timer is added. A new handle to the new timer is returned in either case.\n@param InObj\t\t\t\t\tObject to call the timer function on.\n@param InTimerMethod\t\t\tMethod to call when timer fires.\n@param InRate\t\t\t\tThe amount of time (in seconds) between set and firing.  If <= 0.f, clears existing timers.\n@param InbLoop\t\t\t\ttrue to keep firing at Rate intervals, false to fire only once.\n@param InFirstDelay\t\t\tThe time (in seconds) for the first iteration of a looping timer. If < 0.f InRate will be used."
    },
